      "body": "@gramorris I'm not a GDPR expert, so... a question about this:\r\n\r\n> I don't know if it's possible but it would seem that the possible solution may be to pass bidders through to the cookie sync in url vars. If my observations are correct.\r\n\r\nI thought that GDPR required users to give their consent to _each company_ who wanted to use their personal info. If we added query string param support for bidders, how would the publisher [setting up their AMP page](http://prebid.org/dev-docs/show-prebid-ads-on-amp-pages.html#amp-content-page) know which bidders the user had consented to?",
